args: opentide --json setup ci --help
exit: 0

━━━ stdout
Generate CI/CD pipeline files (platforms discovered from repo config).

Usage: opentide setup ci [OPTIONS] <ci_platform>

Arguments:
  <ci_platform>
          github, gitlab, or azure
          
          [possible values: github, gitlab, azure]

Options:
  -C, --path <PATH>
          Repository path
          
          [default: .]

      --staging, --no-staging
          Deploy to staging tenants from pull requests
          
          [default: staging]

      --inflight, --no-inflight
          Update .opentide/inflight/ preview shards on pull requests
          
          [default: inflight]

      --sharing, --no-sharing
          Share changed objects on the default branch (off unless selected)
          
          [default: no-sharing]

      --lint-changed, --lint-all
          Gate lint on the object files each run changes, so a catalogue with inherited findings can adopt it (validate still checks every file)
          
          [default: lint-all]

      --promotion, --no-promotion
          Write [promotion] enabled in deployment.toml. Omit to keep the repository's setting.

      --promotion-target <PROMOTION_TARGET>
          Status deploy promotes rules to. Omit to keep the repository's setting.

      --python-version <PYTHON_VERSION>
          Python version the pipeline installs
          
          [default: 3.12]

      --explorer-pages, --no-explorer-pages
          Include GitHub Pages explorer build and deploy jobs
          
          [default: no-explorer-pages]

      --variable-group <NAME>
          Azure Pipelines: link this Library variable group in variables: (repeatable; ignored with a warning for github and gitlab)

      --app-token, --no-app-token
          GitHub Actions: the jobs that push to the default branch check out and push with a GitHub App token (variable OPENTIDE_APP_CLIENT_ID, secret OPENTIDE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY) instead of GITHUB_TOKEN; omit to keep what the existing pipeline has (ignored with a warning for gitlab and azure)

      --default-branch <DEFAULT_BRANCH>
          Branch that deploys and receives inflight shards (default: origin/HEAD, then the checked-out branch, then init.defaultBranch, then main; GitLab uses $CI_DEFAULT_BRANCH)

      --stdout
          Print the generated pipeline to stdout and write nothing (to diff it against an adapted one; not with --json or --plan)

      --plan
          List the files each step would write, and write nothing

  -y, --yes
          Write without asking for confirmation

      --help
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide setup ci github --yes

━━━ stderr · empty
